ing  lunch has come a long way i just used to  get a grilled cheese and chocolate milk  school bus is going to be back on the  roads too on monday the district has  between 1500 and 1700 buses running  students and drivers will both wear  masks when they're on the bus and  drivers will also wear face shield when  kids are getting off and on they will  load on one side and then unload on the  other so kids aren't crossing paths  executive director of transportation  jennifer bobis says there's an app that  parents can use to track where their  kids are  we encourage all our parents to download  the onboard bus which allows parents to  track the bus and where it's at and what  time pickup and drop-off is and they get  all the routing information there  now there is a bigger bus driver  shortage than normal so boba says other  people in the school district who have  another job but also a cdl license are  pitching in to help drive  there are plenty of cars to be wary of  two it's been a while since the school  zones were active in some areas so our  traffic anchor nate tannenbaum reminds  us of the school zone rules  well we all should know what the deal is  even if we might be a little out of  practice so whether it's 15 miles an  hour or 20 or maybe 25 miles an hour  when the lights are flashing that's your  speed limit lives are at stake and maybe  the money in your wallet also there are  some other frequently broken rules  around school campuses here's one you're  not supposed to flip u-turns around  school zones you're also not supposed to  pass other vehicles in school zones by  the way school zones are active when  there are three things going on either  when children are present when those  flashing lights are on and it also  includes 30 minutes either before or  after school  back to you  good reminder thank you nate well school  police also say there will be plenty of  first time teen drivers out on the road  so watch for that as well now during the  pandemic school police took the  opportunity to do crisis intervention  training that teaches them to deal with  students who are having mental health  issues now there are concerns there  could be an increase after the pandemic  school police spokesman brian zinke says  their presence will be known on campus  our plan is to have at least two  officers on every single high school  campus and then everyone else will be  supported by our patrol officers they'll  be out patrolling the elementaries and  the middle schools  while a lot of other departments in ccsd  are dealing with larger than normal  staff shortages zinc says ccsd police  are hiring but are only dealing with a  normal amount of officers leaving we'll  changing the grades up next in our back  to school special there will be a new  grading policy this year we break the  differences for you plus what won't be  included in student scores now and which  precautions will be taken on the field  the sports policies to prevent cobit we  are live local now

